title: "Daniel Longitudinal Study"

message: >
If you use or reference this repository, please cite it using the
metadata below. This archive documents a governed, single-subject
longitudinal observation of training exposure, recovery dynamics,
and system-level physiological adaptation.

type: dataset

authors:

- family-names: Hughett
  given-names: Christopher Daniel
  alias: CDHughett

repository-code: https://github.com/CDHughett/daniel-longitudinal-public

abstract: >
The Daniel Longitudinal Study is a governed public archive documenting
continuous single-subject observation across training, recovery,
and behavioral execution. The archive follows an artifact-first model
with retrospective interpretation and explicit structural governance.

keywords:

- longitudinal dataset
- single subject study
- self quantification
- training adaptation
- recovery monitoring
- human performance

